            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to hang on, then the Malayalam for to speed along."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കപ്പൽ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കപ്പൽ — kappal — \"a ship\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തുറമുഖത്ത് ഒരു വലിയ കപ്പൽ വന്നു. tuṟamukhattŭ oru valiya kappal vannu. A big ship came into the harbour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: കപ്പലുകൾ, kappalukaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A small boat is a തോണി; a കപ്പൽ (kappal) crosses the sea."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കപ്പൽ (kappal) is native Dravidian, \"a ship, a sailing vessel\" (DEDR 1219)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
