          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നാവികൻ — nāvikan — \"a sailor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നാവികൻ കപ്പലിൽ നിന്ന് കരയിലേക്ക് ഇറങ്ങി. nāvikan kappalil ninnŭ karayilēkkŭ iṟaṅṅi. The sailor came down from the ship onto the land."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The navy is the നാവികസേന, the sailors' army."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നാവികൻ (nāvikan) is borrowed from Sanskrit nāvika, \"belonging to a boat\", and so a boatman or sailor (Monier-Williams), with the masculine ending -ൻ."
            }
          ]
        },
