          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജെട്ടി — jeṭṭi — \"a jetty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞങ്ങൾ ജെട്ടിയിൽ തോണിക്കായി കാത്തുനിന്നു. ñaṅṅaḷ jeṭṭiyil tōṇikkāyi kāttuninnu. We stood waiting for the boat at the jetty."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Boats on the backwaters stop at a ജെട്ടി (jeṭṭi) the way a bus stops at a stop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജെട്ടി (jeṭṭi) was borrowed from English jetty, a landing stage for boats."
